From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] input: rsinput: quiesce the gamepad MCU across system sleep

The gamepad MCU streams input reports continuously over its geni UART
(measured ~62 irq/s while idle-awake on the Odin 2). Across a system
suspend teardown it keeps sending: qcom_geni_serial_isr() returns
IRQ_NONE once uport->suspended is set, the level line re-fires endlessly
and the spurious-IRQ detector can permanently disable the UART IRQ,
killing the gamepad after resume.

Quiesce the MCU at suspend by dropping its enable and reset GPIOs (the
same lines rsinput_remove() releases), so the UART goes silent before
the serial layer stops servicing it. Resume keeps the existing
init_commands() handshake, which has been proven across many
resume cycles on this hardware.

Companion to the vendor-side approach validated downstream (Pocknix
1004/1006); kept minimal on top of our existing PM ops.
---
--- a/drivers/input/joystick/rsinput.c
+++ b/drivers/input/joystick/rsinput.c
@@ -566,6 +566,19 @@
     struct rsinput_driver *drv = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 
     return rsinput_init_commands(drv);
 }
 
+static int rsinput_suspend(struct device *dev)
+{
+    struct rsinput_driver *drv = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+    if (drv->enable_gpio)
+        gpiod_set_value_cansleep(drv->enable_gpio, 0);
+
+    if (drv->reset_gpio)
+        gpiod_set_value_cansleep(drv->reset_gpio, 0);
+
+    return 0;
+}
+
 static DEFINE_SIMPLE_DEV_PM_OPS(rsinput_pm_ops, NULL, rsinput_resume);
 
 static const struct of_device_id rsinput_of_match[] = {
